insert into public.run_guides (slug, level, position, title, body_md, try_this, is_premium, is_published)
values ('your-first-runs', 'starter', 1, 'Your first runs: why walking is allowed', 'Almost every new runner starts too fast, gets out of breath in two minutes and decides running isn''t for them. The fix is simple: mix running with walking.

Short runs with walking breaks let your heart, lungs, muscles and joints adapt together. Your fitness improves quickly, but tendons and bones take longer, so the plan grows a little each week rather than all at once.

- Run slowly enough that you could chat.
- Walk briskly in the breaks, don''t stop.
- Repeat a week if it felt too hard. That''s progress, not failure.

Consistency beats heroics. Three gentle runs a week for nine weeks will get you further than one exhausting run you never repeat.',
  'Run so slowly on your next run that you could say a full sentence out loud.', false, true)
