insert into public.run_guides (slug, level, position, title, body_md, try_this, is_premium, is_published)
values ('shoes-and-kit', 'starter', 2, 'Shoes and kit: what actually matters', 'You don''t need expensive gear to start, but your shoes matter more than anything else.

- Choose running shoes, not fashion trainers. They are built to cushion and flex at the forefoot.
- Fit is everything: a thumb''s width of space in front of your longest toe, a snug heel, no pressure points.
- Comfort on the first try is the best guide. Pick the pair that feels good, not the one with the most features.
- Replace shoes every 600–800 km, or when the cushioning feels flat.

For clothing, choose light, breathable fabrics that dry quickly rather than cotton, which stays wet and rubs. In hot weather wear a cap and sunscreen. For early or late runs, wear something bright or reflective so drivers see you.',
  'Check your shoes: press the midsole. If it feels hard and creased, plan a replacement.', false, true)
