insert into public.run_guides (slug, level, position, title, body_md, try_this, is_premium, is_published)
values ('easy-pace-talk-test', 'starter', 3, 'The talk test: finding your easy pace', 'Most of your running should be easy, and easy is slower than you think.

The talk test is the simplest guide: at an easy pace you can speak in full sentences. If you can only manage a few words, slow down. If you can sing, you can go a little faster.

Easy running builds the engine: more blood vessels to your muscles, a stronger heart and joints that get used to the impact. It also means you finish wanting more, which is what keeps you coming back.

- Ignore other runners'' speeds; your easy pace is yours.
- Hills, heat and tiredness all make the same pace feel harder, so go by feel.
- It''s fine if your easy pace is close to a fast walk at first.',
  'Say your name and today''s date out loud halfway through your next run.', false, true)
