insert into public.run_guides (slug, level, position, title, body_md, try_this, is_premium, is_published)
values ('breathing-and-side-stitches', 'starter', 5, 'Breathing and side stitches', 'There''s no single correct way to breathe while running. Breathe through your nose and mouth together so you get enough air.

If you''re gasping, you''re going too fast. Slowing down is the best breathing technique there is.

Side stitches are common in new runners. They often come from starting too quickly or eating too close to a run.

- Slow to a walk and breathe out fully and slowly.
- Press gently on the sore spot and lean slightly forward.
- Leave 1–2 hours after a big meal before running.

Relax your shoulders and hands too: tension in your upper body makes breathing shallow.',
  'When you feel tense, drop your shoulders and shake out your hands for a few steps.', false, true)
