insert into public.run_guides (slug, level, position, title, body_md, try_this, is_premium, is_published)
values ('aches-or-injury', 'starter', 6, 'Normal aches or an injury?', 'Some muscle soreness a day or two after a run is normal, especially when you''re new. It feels dull, spreads across a muscle and eases as you warm up.

Pain that signals an injury is different. Stop running and rest if you notice:

- Sharp or stabbing pain, or pain in one precise spot on a bone.
- Pain that gets worse as you run, or makes you limp.
- Swelling, or pain that wakes you at night.

If it hasn''t improved after a few days of rest, see a doctor or physiotherapist. Seek medical help straight away for chest pain, dizziness, fainting or unusual shortness of breath. If you have a heart condition, high blood pressure, are pregnant or have been inactive for a long time, check with your doctor before starting.',
  'After your next run, note any aches in your run notes so you can spot patterns.', false, true)
