insert into public.run_guides (slug, level, position, title, body_md, try_this, is_premium, is_published)
values ('running-form-and-cadence', 'builder', 2, 'Running form and cadence', 'Good form is mostly about being relaxed and light, not copying an elite runner.

- Run tall, with a slight lean from the ankles.
- Let your feet land under your body, not far out in front.
- Keep your arms swinging forward and back, not across your chest.
- Relax your face, hands and shoulders.

Cadence is your number of steps per minute. Many new runners overstride: long, slow steps that land on the heel ahead of the body. Taking slightly quicker, shorter steps (about 5% more) often makes running feel smoother and lowers the load on your knees.

Count your steps for 30 seconds and double it. There''s no magic number; aim to nudge it up gradually, not to hit 180.',
  'Count your steps for 30 seconds, then try a few minutes with slightly quicker, shorter steps.', true, true)
