insert into public.run_guides (slug, level, position, title, body_md, try_this, is_premium, is_published)
values ('pacing-a-race', 'racer', 5, 'How to pace a race', 'The most common race mistake is starting too fast. Adrenaline makes the first kilometres feel easy, and you pay for it later.

- Aim for even pacing, or slightly faster in the second half (a "negative split").
- Run the first kilometre a little slower than goal pace.
- Use your training to choose a realistic goal; your plan''s pace zones can help.
- Check in at halfway: if you feel good, gradually push on.

For a half marathon, the first 10K should feel controlled, almost too easy. The race really begins in the last 5K.',
  'In your next tempo run, deliberately make the second half slightly faster than the first.', true, true)
