insert into public.run_guides (slug, level, position, title, body_md, try_this, is_premium, is_published)
values ('training-with-pace-zones', 'pro', 2, 'Training with pace zones', 'Pace zones turn "easy" and "hard" into numbers that fit your fitness.

Set a goal time in your plan and Goal4Me calculates your zones from it:

- Easy and long: slow and conversational, most of your running.
- Tempo: comfortably hard, roughly the pace you could hold for an hour.
- Intervals: around your current 5K pace.
- Race: your goal pace.

Zones are a guide, not a rule. Heat, hills, wind and fatigue all change what each zone feels like. When pace and effort disagree, trust effort. Update your goal time as you get fitter so the zones keep up.',
  'Set a realistic goal time in your plan settings and check your easy pace.', true, true)
